<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#wa-na">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wa Na</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wa Na is the title of the paramount chief of Wa, a Wala kingdom in the Upper West Region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>. The office rotates among several royal gates, or branches of the ruling family, and the chief rules alongside Muslim office-holders and earth-priests who keep the rites of the land. Wa came under British rule in the 1890s, and the Wa Na remains a traditional ruler today.</p></div>
